Changes.doc:

Here are the changes since the first beta release (v3.01)

v3.03

1. Added multi-selection of files to be processed.  presently, the files
will only show up as marked (asterisked '*') if you don't change file
areas.  in other words, if you change the area, then change back, the files
will not show up as marked, although they actually will be! (this not
*really* what i would call satisfactory, but it's a start)

2. Added 'copy' menu to area editor window.  This menu will allow copying
area data to multiple file areas.  I think the usage is fairly intuitive.
i hope! :-}

3. fixed that little bug which causes pathnames to end up with '//' or ':/'
on the end.... sorry 'bout that :-}

4. added a more useful title to the getlib requester to make it a little
more obvious as to what is being requested.

5. main window now reports the correct version number.

6. added an ABORT button to the runtime message window.

and a few other cosmetic things that aren't really worth mentioning ;-)

v3.04

8.  fixed a bug in the rename function that caused the file list display
entry to appear instead of just the filename.

9.  modified the multi-selection of files.  filemaint can now remember
which files are marked and which are not, although when processing files
(ie move copy etc) only the current area will be processed for now...

10.  file descriptions can now be changed from the gui.  (i don't really
like this method much, but it will have to do for now):

11.  re-arranged the windows a bit.

12.  added a range selection to enable partial area processing.

13.  removed *lots* of stupid bugs! :-}

v3.05, 3.06, 3.07:

14.  i changed a few things here and there, and added some more buttons and
rearranged the window layouts a bit.

15.  i found a problem with the 'copy' and 'move' functions which crashed
many systems.  thanks to kev tankard for bringing it to my attention!

16. fixed a terrible error in the code that caused some systems (especially
a1200 it seems) to hang on initial startup :-}

v3.08

17. added a new option to the configuration setting to enable the uploader
names to be displayed in the file lists.

** IMPORTANT NOTE!! ** due to some reshuffling of the configuration file
flags, you will need to reset the flags in the config editor.  just load up
the filemaint (GUI) configuration editor and set the flags according to your
system requirements.

18. there is now a cut-down version of the filemaint code called "fm" that
contains only the code needed for running the bbs functions.  ** WARNING **
there is NO guarantee that future versions will be "cross comapatable with
their full-blown counterparts!  therefore if you intend to use the
mini-filemaint for bbs functions, always make sure that it is the same
version as the full FileMaint program.

v3.09

19. the show-uploader-name configuration flag now also effects the
description view in the GUI description listview.

20. offline files will show up as such in the GUI listview now.

21. a new config flag will now optionally remove the "bloody awful view
transfer details" message.  (not *my* words! ;-)

22. ranges now work correctly for 'adopt' and 'sort' functions.

23. added 'show uploader name' switch to commandline options.  the switch
'-u' will disable (override) showing uploader name in the file lists, and
the switch '+u' will force the feature on.

24. you will now be prompted first before processing multiple file areas
from the GUI.

25. rexx functions are no longer available in the 'cut-down' version (fm).
if you wish to use the arexx support, you must run the full version of
FileMaint.

v3.10

26.  fixed a small but annoying bug that made it impossible to save archive
type settings.

27.  fixed a bug that would crash a local line when marking files.  

v3.11

28.  rearranged some code to improve startup speed.

29.  the cut-down 'fm' may now be made resident for that extra bit of
speed if necessary.

v3.12

*note*: due to the foolish loss of some of the source code, i hope that this
version is not a step backwards! ;-}  there are, however, quite a few
enhancements nonetheless, including these things:

30. a new gui has been created, as i lost all the data for the last one.
it looks mostly the same, but it ought to fit into a standard workbench
screen now :-}

31.  the runtime message window now remains open when processing is in
progress.

32. when moving all files out from a particular area, the description goes
too ;-)

33. the 'abort' gadget on the runtime message window actually works now.

v3.13

34. fixed that annoying 'makedir failed' message :-}

35. fixed the config editor window so that maxmarked and max desclines
comes up as it should.

36. added a new flag to the file areas editor 'free download' flag.  when
checked, filemaint will not check a user's file credits for any file in
that area, although download time will be estimated and checked for
overtime.

37. changed how areas and arcs config names are kept.  from now on, this
information is kept in the configuration structure.  therefore, filemaint
only keeps track of one env variable (being 'config' name and path).

38. an advantage of the above is that you can now define a particular
configuration setup on the commandline under the '-c<configfile>' switch.

39. when pressing (s)top while processing multiple areas (eg
"filemaint l20-239") filemaint used to open all list files causing a delay
before closing.  this problem has now been fixed.

v3.14

40. fixed a bug that caused a **NULL POINTER** reference when displaying
custom file headers.

41. interactive mode now lists the entire file list (including the last
page or part thereof)

42. fixed a bug (i think) in download ratio calculations.  users who have not
uploaded anything, may download up to the number of k defined by their byte
ratio when STRICTDL is turned *off* - eg: if a user has uploaded nothing,
but has a byte ratio of 5:1, they may download up to 5k of files before
needing to upload.
byte ratio and/or file ratio equal to zero disables that ratio.

43. fixed a minor problem with the range gadgets in the gui maintainence
window.  changing the 'to' field in the librange arguments used to cause
the 'from' argument to be changed to that same value.

44.  custom (and default) header will now reflect proper file area names in
interactive mode.

v3.15

45.  finally fixed that bug with the 'strictdl' - seems that i had it all
backwards.  with strictdl turned ON, fm would behave as if it were OFF and
vice-versa :-}  i have put it right now! :)

**KNOWN BUGS:
*here is a list of *known* bugs - i will fix them as soon as i get around
to it! :-}  If you discover a bug that is not listed here, then please inform
me asap!

-> 'insert' new file area in area editor doesn't work properly.

-> maximum file area name length is 32 characters.  (and dir path) - longer
names will cause problems.

-> sorting large areas causes a stack overflow.

**Things to do:
*These are some things that have been suggested by users of filemaint, or
things that i want to do in the near future (or both!).  If there is
something else that you'd like to see here, please send mail to one of the
addresses below.

-> fix the above things! ;-)

-> activate generate fullist

-> user-configurable interactive menu

-> user-configurable file lists

-> debug output to file?

-> add routine to keep track of average transfer times to allow for more
accurate transfer time estimates.

-> find area by dir.

-> add file area grouping system.

-> add an option to list files using a 'scroller' approach.

Cheers,  Mike Everest.


